 "gaps": "1) RESOLVED (was: Faour thesis not retrieved). The thesis was retrieved from https://reductions.network/papers/faour_extending_reductions_network_a_survey_of_parameterized_complexity and independently confirms the parameterized network as exactly 29 problems in the same three classes. See networks.parameterized.thesis_cross_check. ONE conflict remains unresolved between the two sources: Monotone Prenex CNF Query Non-Emptiness is tagged {W[1]-hard, W[2]} in the repo but is defined in the thesis's \"W[1]-Complete Problems\" section with \"Complete for: W[1].\" Both cite Downey, Fellows & Taylor (DMTCS 1996). Since W[1] subseteq W[2] the repo tag is not false, only weaker; the thesis value is the better-sourced one. Both are recorded; neither was overwritten. 2) The repo `# completeness` field records membership and hardness as separate tokens. 'W[1]'+'W[1]-hard' is read here as W[1]-complete. For the 13 problems the repo tags 'W[2]'+'W[1]-hard', the repo itself does NOT assert W[2]-hardness; the Faour thesis does assert W[2]-completeness for 12 of them (all but the Monotone Prenex case above). `completeness_raw` preserves the exact repo tokens and `thesis_complete_for` the thesis's. 3) Six classic vertices are unfilled stubs in the repo - instances/solutions/citations literally 'todo' and empty completeness: Chinese Postman, Directed Rural Postman, Undirected Rural Postman, Minimal Maximal Matching, s-t-Max Cut. A further five carry no completeness value: Edge Dominating Set, Longest Common Subsequence, Not-All-Equal 4SAT, Planar Vertex Cover, Vertex Cover on Cubic Graph. These are genuine vertices but the source establishes no complexity value for them. 4) Counts differ slightly from the ~57/~23/~29 in the tasking. Classic is 58, not 57: Figure 1 renders 57 legible labels because two distinct vertices both abbreviate to 'MLST' (Maximum Leaf Spanning Tree and Minimum Leaf Spanning Tree) and 'EXACT COVER' (EC) is drawn occluded behind the '3-Dim Matching' node; GRAPH COLORING is in the repo but was not located in the figure. The repo listing (58) is authoritative over the figure. Approximation is 23 after excluding the byte-identical duplicate `dominating_set_TEST.md`. 5) The approximation network's `# completeness` field only ever records the hardness FRAMEWORK ('PCP' and/or 'UGC'), never a ratio or an APX-class. No inapproximability CONSTANT can be read off this source for any of the 23 approximation vertices; the per-problem citations (Hastad 2001, Khot 2002, Feige 1998, Vazirani 2001, Williamson-Shmoys 2011, Austrin 2007, Crescenzi-Silvestri-Trevisan 2001) are the only place those live, and they were not opened. 6) Four approximation vertices carry NO citation at all (empty `# citations`): Maximum Satisfiability with three literals pro clause (Max-3sat), Satisfiability problem, Vertex Cover, Weighted Maximum Cut, Weighted Vertex Cover. 7) Vertex counts are as of data-repo commit 8089fb4f3b0d674550ce00449d41533b0d7e3404 (2025-12-13); the live site may have drifted since."
